<title>BULGARIA: BULGARIA 89-DAY T-BILLS SOLD OUT, YIELD 60 PCT.</title>
<headline>BULGARIA 89-DAY T-BILLS SOLD OUT, YIELD 60 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry offer</p>
<p>of 25 billion levs of 89-day floater coupon T-bills was sold</p>
<p>out, yielding 60.23 percent until maturity, the Bulgarian</p>
<p>National Bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no minimum acceptable price set</p>
<p>in advance by the ministry for Monday's auction. Markets were</p>
<p>closed in Bulgaria from Tuesday through Thursday for the New</p>
<p>Year.</p>
<p>The coupon was set equal to the BNB's central interest rate</p>
<p>(CIR) for the period to maturity. The CIR is now set at 15</p>
<p>percent monthly or 180 percent annually.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices are in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		     BG 3010097023</p>
<p> Auction date		     December 30, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date			 January 3, 1997</p>
<p> Maturity date		    April 2, 1997</p>
<p> Bids received		    25.25 bln levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids		89.30 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		    25 bln levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	     89.80 pct</p>
<p> Average yield to maturity    60.23 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
</text>
